  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Heat Advisories are in effect for portions of the\nCWA Tues and Wed. Upgrade to Warnings possible on WED for the \nLower Susq.\n\nThe only message today is the expansion and addition to the heat\nadvisories for Tues and Wed. The area covered by Tues's advy\nincreased by one county (Huntingdon). After collaboration with\nour neighboring offices, we decided to issue an advisory for the\nSE half of the area for Wed. So, some of the area active on Tues\nnow doesn't get out of the advy until Wed evening. But, the heat\nindex values do go down in the north on Wed, but up a little in\nthe south. This was rather expected, but the confidence was not\nhigh enough until now to make that call. There is still a chance\n(I'd give it a 40% chc) that we may end up upgrading a small\nportion of the Wed advy to a warning (Lanc/Leb/York/Dauph are\nmost-possible). \n\nThe arrival of slightly drier and cooler air and increased\nclouds on Wed and further advancement to the S on Thurs should\nhelp keep the heat index values down in the sub-advy range.",
